+Follow up the overly restrictive immutable-slot policy in 0024.
+Share live MAC slots by reference count and cache unused slots for reuse.
+Use slot 0 and unregistered GDM indices as well as 5..14, while keeping
+registered GDM base slots and KEEP separate. Reclaim least-recently released
+slots only after their last software flow and checked hardware invalidation.
+Quarantine only slots with failed UPDMEM writes or uncertain flow deletion.
+
+Acquire after validation/allocation and release on insertion failure or
+deletion. Before rebinding a flow to another hardware hash, invalidate its
+old binding; retain the old hash if that fails. Track a timed-out new bind
+for later cleanup. Avoid overwriting a hardware entry that has aged/reused.
+The normal packet forwarding path does not maintain slot references.
